"stores": "key,name,kind,list_threshold_meals,countdown,cadence,note\ncostco,Warehouse club,warehouse,21,yes,\"every 21+ days, stretched when possible\",\"Costco, Sam's Club or BJ's: big packs sized for a 21-day cycle; every rotation protein freezes, so stretching to three weeks is free (spec section 7). Switch it off under Profile if you have none; the grocery store carries everything\"\npublix,Grocery store,grocery,10,no,weekly,\"Any supermarket: Publix, Kroger, Safeway, Walmart, Aldi, Trader Joe's. The weekly run for what big packs outlive, and every item the rotation uses when there is no warehouse club. The weekly-ad feature was removed on purpose; do not rebuild it (spec section 7)\"\n",
"flavor_pantry": "id,name,note\r\ngh,G Hughes BBQ + teriyaki,\"Sugar free, essentially free calories.\"\r\nfr,Frank's RedHot,Buffalo nights.\r\nsm,\"Salsa, dijon, spicy mustard\",\"Bowls, tacos, sausage nights.\"\r\nrs,Ranch seasoning packets,Dust on meat; in yogurt it becomes the dip.\r\nms,Montreal + cajun/blackening seasoning,Steak and fish nights.\r\nsp,Smoked paprika · chili · cumin · granulated garlic · lemon pepper,Five jars behind every kit — and five plants your gut counts.\r\nsw,Honey · cinnamon · cocoa powder · sugar-free syrup,\"The bowl is dessert. Honey measured, the rest free.\"\r\nol,\"Olives, pickles\",Fat slot texture. Keeps forever.\r\n",
"equipment": "id,name,modes,note\nminioven,Countertop oven,Air Fry|Roast|Air Broil|Bake,\"A CHEF iQ MiniOven or any countertop air-fryer oven of about 25 qt, with a basket, a pan and racks; three rack positions. No stovetop\"\nmicrowave,Microwave,Micro,Rice pouches and beans in 90 seconds; Plan B cooks entirely here\noven,Oven,Bake|Roast|Broil,\"A full-size oven; a sheet pan and foil are all it needs. Roast means the convection or fan setting where there is one, else Bake at the same temperature\"\nstovetop,Stovetop,Pan|Simmer|Boil,\"A skillet and a pot. Boiled potatoes stand in for roasted ones\"\nairfryer,Air fryer,Air Fry|Roast|Bake,\"A basket air fryer, 4 to 6 qt. Two portions fill it; three or four cook in batches\"\nslowcooker,Slow cooker,Low|High,\"A 6-quart slow cooker: one pot holds four portions, so a household needs no second batch. Start it four to eight hours before dinner; rice, pasta and tortillas are done on the side, as the meal says\"\n",
