"profile": "key,value\ndob,\nsex,\ndraw_cadence_months,6\nnear_limit_pct,10\nrisk_tier,intermediate\nrisk_tier_note,Options: low | borderline | intermediate | high | very_high (2026 ACC/AHA PREVENT 10-yr risk: <3% | 3-<5% | 5-<10% | >=10% | established ASCVD). Set from the PREVENT calculator (professional.heart.org/en/guidelines-and-statements/prevent-calculator) or your clinician. 'intermediate' is the guideline default used by the research.\nguideline_lens,\nguideline_lens_note,\"conventional = targets from major clinical guidelines (ACC/AHA, ESC/EAS, ADA, KDIGO, Endocrine Society...), graded by evidence. functional = 'optimal' ranges published by functional/longevity-medicine sources, each attributed and graded (outcome data / observational / expert opinion). Both are always shown; this setting chooses which one judges your values and drives the plan.\"\nstores,\nstore_picks,\nstores_note,\"stores = the stores you shop, in the order you would rather buy from, separated by |, e.g. costco|publix (empty means every store in stores.csv, in its order). store_picks = where to buy an item that more than one of those stores carries, e.g. fairlife:publix|eggs:costco. Both are edited from Profile in the app.\"\nweight_lb,\nheight_in,\nactivity,\ngoal,\nrate,\nbody_note,\"About you, asked on first run and changed under Profile, Your target: weight_lb, height_in, activity (sedentary | light | moderate | active | very_active), goal (hold | lose | gain), rate (gentle | steady). With dob and sex above, the app estimates the day's calories and protein (Mifflin-St Jeor times the activity factor, then the goal's deficit; protein 0.8 g per lb) and writes them to diet.csv, and sizes the plate from them. An estimate is within about 15 percent for any one person; the scale corrects it.\"\n",
